    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0012" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.N.C./161: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-21T15:00:00-03:00">January 21, 1941—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Department’s telegram 23, January 16, 9 p.m. For the Under Secretary from
                    Fenwick. Security Zone Convention already adopted by Neutrality Committee before
                    receipt of telegram under reference. Would call attention, however, to fact that
                    Habana Meeting<anchor n="6" xml:id="d3-f1"/> asked Committee to submit merely a
                    preliminary draft, permitting inference that governments would want to suggest
                    changes before final draft submitted to signature. Hence the Department is
                    entirely free to suggest alterations in the text. I would recommend,
                    nevertheless, that instead of attempting to alter phrases in the convention, to
                    prevent obvious conflicts with pending legislation, the Department could shelve
                    the whole convention by delaying its return to the Committee. Committee will
                    submit draft convention to Pan-American Union as confidential documents, with
                    the request that the Union transmit it to the American Governments as
                    confidential. Can delay arrival of convention at the Pan-American Union at least
                    1 month. [Fenwick.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
